-Completing a reset is not implemented yet.
+## Reset flow
+
+1. `request_reset(email)` issues a new reset token for the account and
+   records when it was issued. Requesting again issues an additional
+   token; every outstanding token for the account is valid until it is
+   used, expires, or a reset completes.
+2. `complete_reset(email, token, new_password)` verifies the token, then:
+   - Rejects the token if it is unknown, expired, or does not match a
+     token issued for that account.
+   - Enforces that tokens are **single use**: once a reset completes, all
+     outstanding tokens for the account (including the one just used) are
+     cleared, so none of them can be reused.
+   - Enforces that tokens **expire 30 minutes** after they were issued.
+   - On success, hashes and stores the new password and returns `True`.
+   - On any failure (unknown, expired, or already-used token), returns
+     `False`. It never raises for these cases, so callers can't use
+     exception type to probe why a token was rejected.
+3. `check_token(email, token)` is a read-only check of whether a token is
+   currently valid (issued, unexpired, and not yet consumed by a
+   completed reset), without consuming it.
